{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174459-werewolf-gmc-stop-gap","id":174459,"title":"Werewolf GMC Stop Gap","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-19T12:50:52-07:00","id":174459,"title":"Werewolf GMC Stop Gap","content":"I run about a month now a post GMC <b>Forsaken</b> game. As mostly I use the spoilers from <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> to make a patch there is one problem I have - Experience Costs. On next session I need new Rituals to use. How much should they cost? And as I'm with it, I will make my proposal on costs in general - based on <b>God Machine Chronicles</b> and <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b>.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Werewolf Experience Costs post GMC rules</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b> - 4 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Skill</b> - 2 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Rite</b> - 1 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Gift</b> - 4 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Primal Urge</b> - 5 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Harmony</b> - 2 Experience per dot<br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> Should <i>Itheaur</i> get two dots of Ritual per Experience point as Auspice power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-19-2014, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:09:36-07:00","id":174493,"title":"","content":"With the new Harmony system I don't know if it makes sense to buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:34:06-07:00","id":174512,"title":"","content":"Yep, I think they said Harmony was not bought now. You have to go out of your way to get Breaking points towards the extreme you want to get back into balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:48:29-07:00","id":174521,"title":"","content":"Okay, Harmony is not buy-able. But are Rites and Gifts prices correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:56:12-07:00","id":174540,"title":"","content":"Yep, the rest seems fine. I'm not sure about Rites, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T15:44:53-07:00","id":174654,"title":"","content":"A dot of rites should cost 2xp, come with a freebie. Individual rites prolly cost 1xp.<br /> <br /> Unlocking an affinity gift is prolly gonna cost 3xp, individual facets 2xp. Make that 4 and 3 with non affinity. Affinity renown is gonna cost 3xp, non affinity 4xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T03:04:10-07:00","id":257129,"title":"","content":"As my players gone with Death Rage as tactics to solve they problems, I make quick rules for Death Rage based on <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-red-mist-descends/\" target=\"_blank\">Red Mist spoiler</a>. Here is table of time the Rage last:<br /> <br /> Primal Urge - Time of Death Rage<br /> 1 - 5 minutes<br /> 2 - 10 minutes<br /> 3 - 30 minutes<br /> 4 - 1 hour<br /> 5 - 2 hours<br /> 6 - 4 hours<br /> 7 - 6 hours<br /> 8 - 8 hours<br /> 9 - 10 hours<br /> 10 - 12 hours<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:30:19-08:00","id":362546,"title":"","content":"How much cost a Renowns for GMC rules? 4XP for affinity ones, 5XP for non-affinity ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:38:12-08:00","id":362553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174459-werewolf-gmc-stop-gap?p=362546#post362546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much cost a Renowns for GMC rules? 4XP for affinity ones, 5XP for non-affinity ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds pricy. I'd go with 2XP and 3XP myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:07:44-08:00","id":362589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174459-werewolf-gmc-stop-gap?p=362553#post362553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds pricy. I'd go with 2XP and 3XP myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what? They were x6 and x8 in 1ed Werewolf.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:19:25-08:00","id":362596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174459-werewolf-gmc-stop-gap?p=362589#post362589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on what? They were x6 and x8 in 1ed Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Power stats tend to require 5XP, so Renown shouldn't be as costly. Didn't want to do 3XP and 4XP because that still sounded costly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:29:26-08:00","id":362630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174459-werewolf-gmc-stop-gap?p=362589#post362589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on what? They were x6 and x8 in 1ed Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>They used to give a Gift dot in 1e, which is why they were the cost of a Gift dot plus a little bit.<br /> <br /> They now give a Facet rather than unlocking a whole Gift, but then Renown dots are also more meaningful now in terms of the benefits they give you.<br /> <br /> Your 4/5XP guestimate is too high. OTOH I don't want to give the actual numbers since we're pretty close to the actual release these days and there'll hardly be anything new in the book if we just keep spoiling everything beforehand <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T12:28:56-08:00","id":362801,"title":"","content":"As much sense as it made to have them at x6 and x8 in 1e, it made renown an exp blackhole for your character. Plus you ran into some interesting problems where the character will have done something that totally deserves a renown point, but they just don't have the experience to spend on it or have something else they want more. I'm currently running a werewolf who easily can justify getting up to Glory 4, but I've been sitting at Glory 0 for a year and a half now because frankly I just don't have the exp to raise a x8 stat and I have stats that are more important to my character to invest in. So there's a bit of a dissonance between the principle and the practice of renown.<br /> <br /> Small rant about the old system aside, I think some kind of system where werewolves can get bonus exp for doing renown/hunting/werewolf stuff would alleviate a lot of the problems of having an extra stat on top of everything else that has to be invested into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T12:54:30-08:00","id":362820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174459-werewolf-gmc-stop-gap?p=362630#post362630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They used to give a Gift dot in 1e, which is why they were the cost of a Gift dot plus a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reasoning for that was this, as I can only read <b>Werewolf</b> 1ed rules, not like Firstborns like developers that have secrets of 2ed... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174459-werewolf-gmc-stop-gap?p=362630#post362630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They now give a Facet rather than unlocking a whole Gift, but then Renown dots are also more meaningful now in terms of the benefits they give you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in 2ed characters buy Gifts list and Facet separately? Like when I want my Uratha to learn Weather Gifts general list I pay Y XP to unlock the list and when I want to learn a Wisdom Facet of this Gift I pay Z XP? To learn totally new Facet of new Gift I did not have I need Z+Y XP to pay?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174459-werewolf-gmc-stop-gap?p=362630#post362630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your 4/5XP guestimate is too high. OTOH I don't want to give the actual numbers since we're pretty close to the actual release these days and there'll hardly be anything new in the book if we just keep spoiling everything beforehand <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We talk here about fan &quot;patch&quot; to play 1ed-ish <b>Werewolf</b> with GMC rules here, so it's hardly &quot;oh, those will be official rules&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just run game on GMC ruleset, and my players want to buy new Renowns now, not after next half year when 2ed will come out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A year ago <b>DaveB</b> putted <b>Mage</b> GMC Stop Gap and openly wrote that some of this rules are totally in contradiction to those that will be in 2ed <b>Mage</b>. And I think we can talk in this spirit of &quot;uncannon&quot;, totally fan like costs and little tweaks to general quick patch for 1.5 ed. So in this spirit you think a 2/3 XP is better number for Renown?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-07-2015, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T20:25:36-08:00","id":363171,"title":"","content":"I believe werewolves have to buy access to a Shadow Gift before they can learn any of its facets. A werewolf starts with access to some Shadow Gifts (not sure how many) based on tribe and auspice, so it's not really much different than vampires having to pay more for out-of-clan Disciplines. It's just that werewolves make a one time payment instead of paying extra for each dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}